## 8. Node.js rewrite (2026-11-13)
Change: the server was rewritten from Rust to Node.js (owner decision,
2026-11-13: target dev machines usually have Node already, so the tool runs
on top of it). Stack: node-pty (PTY), ws (WebSocket), smol-toml (config).
Entry point src/server.js; UI src/ui.html is unchanged. The Rust
implementation is preserved on the `rust-impl` branch (at 194c8bf).

Environment: Linux (x86_64 VM), Node v24.22.1, npm 10.9.4.

8a. Install: `npm install` — ws 8.x, smol-toml, node-pty 1.1.0 installed.
    VM-specific note: node-gyp's own header download failed on this VM
    (its tar extraction hits "EPERM: operation not permitted, fchown" on
    this filesystem), so the headers were extracted manually and the
    install was run with npm_config_nodedir set. node-pty then built and
    loads, and a spawn smoke test printed the expected output. On a normal
    machine the plain `npm install` path (prebuild or node-gyp) applies.
8b. Automated harness (~/workspace/bt-verify/run-verify.js, 30 checks, all
    PASS), same coverage as sections 2-6:
    Run A (fresh config auto-created, port 17337, api_enabled=false):
    config created with a generated token, permissions 0600; GET / no
    token 401 / ?token 200 / Bearer 200 / wrong token 401; /api/sessions
    404 while disabled; /sessions without token 401. Two WS sessions with
    distinct ids; `echo BT_OK_$((12340+5))` -> "BT_OK_12345"; session1
    `cd /tmp; pwd` -> /tmp while session2 `pwd` -> /home/hatch (independent
